# African Childrens Choir Concert - Under One Sky

Sunshine Coast residents will be treated to a unique musical experience when the African Children’s Choir returns with its vibrant and outstanding musical and dancing performance at Lake Kawana Community Centre in June. The concert will be an exclusive double bill, featuring highly acclaimed dynamic looping artist Mr Percival as support act, with guest appearance by Cool Harmonies Community Choir. The African Children’s Choir is comprised of orphaned and vulnerable children from the disadvantaged Kampala and Luwero areas of Uganda. Their vibrancy, outstanding musical and dancing abilities have captured the world’s imagination since the choir started touring North America and Europe 30 years ago to raise money for children’s education. The African Children’s Choir is returning to Australia following its inaugural visit in 2013, with sell out concerts and workshops across eastern Australia, including the Sunshine Coast. Cool Harmonies community choir will again host the 18 children and eight chaperones from the Uganda-based choir who will present a fun filled evening of singing, drumming and dancing as they spread their message of hope and joy for their future. The Sunshine Coast visit is part of a three-month tour across three States, visiting Geelong, Melbourne, Albury, Canberra, Wollongong, Sydney, Nowra, Laurieton, Port Macquarie, Taree, Bellingen, Mullumbimby, Gold Coast, and Brisbane. Meet the kids preparing for their tour to Australia:[http://vimeo.com/98395905](http://l.facebook.com/l.php?u=http%3A%2F%2Fvimeo.com%2F98395905&h=zAQFcrxTq&enc=AZOefAh2NmvVH7YdcZX93ENvvA4VimmxwaLmy_TrEAVTyi8iQXwxrd5xmKLUrJ-rR0g&s=1) Under One Sky Concert Where: Lake Kawana Community Centre When: Saturday, 20 June 2015 Time: 7pm - 9pm Tickets $30 Adult $25 Concession $25 Students $20 Children (5-12yrs) $270 Adult Group 10 $225 Concession Group 10 $60 Family of 3 (1 Adult & 2 children or 2 adults and 1 child) $90 Family of 4 (min 2 children) $105 Family of 5 (min 2 adults) There will now be a yummy menu at the show! So come on down early and join us for some fun! Lake Kawana Community Centre will have caterer’s supplying food & drinks for purchase on the night of the African Children’s Choir – Under One Sky Concert! Canteen Choice of Ugandan Inspired Foods Veggie Samosa $5 Chicken Curry and Rice $10 Veggie Curry and Rice $10 (Coast local inspired) Macadamia Brownie $5 Water bottle $2 So come on down from 5.00pm onwards and soak up the atmosphere of the live performances in the courtyard while enjoying your meal before the show. Can’t wait to see you there!
